## 1. What is the book about?

Being alone and feeling lonely are not the same thing.

- Loneliness is the painful feeling of disconnection, even when other people may be around.
- Solitude is the experience of spending time alone by choice, using that time to reflect, recharge, learn, or enjoy your own interests.

The book's central message is that you don't need to fill every quiet moment with another person's attention. You can develop self-awareness, emotional independence, and confidence while still valuing friendship, love, and human connection.

The goal isn't to stop needing people. It's to stop abandoning yourself just to keep other people around.

