## 3. Loneliness versus solitude

Loneliness

Feeling disconnected or unwanted

Seeking connection but struggling to find it

Feeling isolated even among people

Healthy solitude

Enjoying time with yourself

Reflecting and recharging by choice

Remaining open to meaningful connection

The important distinction is that solitude is not about rejecting everyone. It is about being able to spend time alone without feeling that your life has less value.

